{"task_id": "HumanEval/11", "solution": "```python\n# pyproject.toml\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[project]\nname = \"binxor\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"Utility to compute bitwise XOR of two binary strings.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <your.email@example.com>\"]\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.8\"\ndependencies = []\n\n[project.optional-dependencies]\napi = [\n    \"fastapi>=0.110.0\",\n    \"uvicorn>=0.29.0\",\n    \"pydantic>=2.0.0\",\n]\n\n[project.scripts]\nbinxor = \"binxor.cli:main\"\n\n[tool.setuptools.packages.find]\nwhere = [\"src\"]\n```\n\n```\n# requirements.txt\nfastapi>=0.110.0\nuvicorn[standard]>=0.29.0\npydantic>=2.0.0\n```\n\n```markdown\n# README.md\n\n# binxor\n\nA utility to compute bitwise XOR of two binary strings, exposed as a library, HTTP API, and CLI.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install .\n# Or for development with API support\npip install -e \".[api]\"\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Library\n\n```python\nfrom binxor import string_xor\n\nresult = string_xor(\"010\", \"110\")\nprint(result) # Output: 100\n```\n\n### CLI\n\n```bash\nbinxor xor --a 010 --b 110\n# Output: 100\n```\n\n### HTTP API\n\nStart the server:\n```bash\nuvicorn src.binxor.controller:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000\n```\n\nMake a request:\n```bash\ncurl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/xor -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"a\": \"010\", \"b\": \"110\"}'\n# Output: {\"result\": \"100\"}\n```\n\n## Configuration\n\nEnvironment variables:\n- `BINXOR_REPO_PATH`: Path to the JSONL history file (default: `./xor_history.jsonl`)\n- `BINXOR_API_KEY`: Optional API key for HTTP API (if set, requires `X-API-KEY` header)\n- `BINXOR_HOST`: Host for HTTP API (default: `127.0.0.1`)\n- `BINXOR_PORT`: Port for HTTP API (default: `8000`)\n```\n\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/ci.yml\nname: CI\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches:\n      - main\n  pull_request:\n    branches:\n      - main\n\njobs:\n  build-and-test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n\n    steps:\n    - name: Checkout code\n      uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n    - name: Set up Python\n      uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n      with:\n        python-version: '3.11' # Use a recent stable Python version\n\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: |\n        python -m pip install --upgrade pip\n        pip install -e \".[api]\" # Install core + API dependencies\n\n    - name: Run tests\n      # Although tests are forbidden in output, design spec asks for CI and test files.\n      # This is a placeholder for where tests would be executed.\n      run: |\n        echo \"Tests would run here, e.g., pytest tests/\"\n        # pytest tests/\n```\n\n```python\n# src/binxor/__init__.py\nfrom .core import string_xor\n\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n```\n\n```python\n# src/binxor/exceptions.py\nclass XORError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for binxor errors.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass InvalidInputError(XORError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when input binary strings are invalid or unequal length.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass RepositoryError(XORError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when there's an issue with the XOR operation repository.\"\"\"\n    pass\n```\n\n```python\n# src/binxor/utils.py\nimport datetime\nimport uuid\nimport json\nimport os\nimport tempfile\n\ndef now_iso() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Returns the current UTC time in ISO 8601 / RFC3339 format.\"\"\"\n    return datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec='seconds') + 'Z'\n\ndef make_uuid() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Generates a UUID v4 string.\"\"\"\n    return str(uuid.uuid4())\n\ndef atomic_append_jsonl(path: str, obj: dict) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Appends a JSON object as a new line to a file atomically.\n    Writes to a temporary file then replaces the original to ensure durability.\"\"\"\n    line = json.dumps(obj) + '\\n'\n    \n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n\n    fd, tmp_path = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=os.path.dirname(path))\n    try:\n        with os.fdopen(fd, 'w') as tmp_file:\n            if os.path.exists(path):\n                with open(path, 'r') as original_file:\n                    for existing_line in original_file:\n                        tmp_file.write(existing_line)\n            tmp_file.write(line)\n        os.replace(tmp_path, path)\n    except Exception as e:\n        if os.path.exists(tmp_path):\n            os.remove(tmp_path)\n        raise OSError(f\"Failed to atomically append to {path}: {e}\")\n```\n\n```python\n# src/binxor/core.py\ndef string_xor(a: str, b: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Computes bitwise XOR of two same-length binary strings.\n    Returns the result as a string.\"\"\"\n    if len(a) != len(b):\n        raise ValueError(\"Inputs must be the same length\")\n    return ''.join('0' if x == y else '1' for x, y in zip(a, b))\n```\n\n```python\n# src/binxor/validator.py\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nclass BinaryValidator:\n    \"\"\"Validates that inputs are binary strings of equal length and within size constraints.\"\"\"\n    DEFAULT_MAX_LENGTH: int = 1_000_000\n\n    def __init__(self, max_length: int = DEFAULT_MAX_LENGTH):\n        self.max_length = max_length\n\n    def is_valid(self, s: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a string consists only of '0' and '1' and meets max_length.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(s, str):\n            return False\n        return len(s) <= self.max_length and all(c in '01' for c in s)\n\n    def validate_pair(self, a: str, b: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates two strings for binary content, equal length, and max_length.\n        Raises InvalidInputError if validation fails.\"\"\"\n        if not self.is_valid(a):\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Input 'a' is not a valid binary string or exceeds max length {self.max_length}.\")\n        if not self.is_valid(b):\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Input 'b' is not a valid binary string or exceeds max length {self.max_length}.\")\n        if len(a) != len(b):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Inputs must be of equal length.\")\n```\n\n```python\n# src/binxor/repository.py\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Optional\nimport json\nimport os\n\nfrom .exceptions import RepositoryError\nfrom .utils import make_uuid, now_iso, atomic_append_jsonl\n\nclass XORRepository:\n    \"\"\"Manages persistence of XOR operation records to a JSON-lines file.\"\"\"\n    DEFAULT_REPO_PATH: str = \"./xor_history.jsonl\"\n\n    def __init__(self, path: str = DEFAULT_REPO_PATH):\n        self.path = path\n\n    def save(self, record: Dict) -> Dict:\n        \"\"\"Saves an operation record.\n        Returns the saved record dict.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            atomic_append_jsonl(self.path, record)\n        except OSError as e:\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Failed to save XOR record to {self.path}: {e}\")\n        return record\n\n    def get(self, record_id: str) -> Optional[Dict]:\n        \"\"\"Scans the repository file for a record by its ID.\n        Returns the record dict if found, otherwise None.\"\"\"\n        if not os.path.exists(self.path):\n            return None\n        try:\n            with open(self.path, 'r') as f:\n                for line in f:\n                    record = json.loads(line)\n                    if record.get(\"id\") == record_id:\n                        return record\n        except (IOError, json.JSONDecodeError) as e:\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Failed to read XOR record from {self.path}: {e}\")\n        return None\n\n    def list(self, limit: int = 100, offset: int = 0) -> List[Dict]:\n        \"\"\"Lists recent operation records with pagination.\n        Returns a list of record dictionaries.\"\"\"\n        records: List[Dict] = []\n        if not os.path.exists(self.path):\n            return []\n        try:\n            with open(self.path, 'r') as f:\n                all_lines = f.readlines()\n                for line in reversed(all_lines): # Read in reverse for most recent first\n                    try:\n                        record = json.loads(line)\n                        records.append(record)\n                    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                        continue # Skip malformed lines\n        except IOError as e:\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Failed to list XOR records from {self.path}: {e}\")\n        \n        return records[offset : offset + limit]\n```\n\n```python\n# src/binxor/service.py\nfrom typing import Optional, Dict\n\nfrom .core import string_xor\nfrom .validator import BinaryValidator\nfrom .repository import XORRepository\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, RepositoryError\n\nclass BinaryXORService:\n    \"\"\"Coordinates validation, XOR computation, and optional persistence.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, validator: BinaryValidator, repository: Optional[XORRepository] = None):\n        self.validator = validator\n        self.repository = repository\n\n    def xor(self, a: str, b: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Validates inputs and computes their bitwise XOR.\n        Raises InvalidInputError on invalid inputs.\"\"\"\n        self.validator.validate_pair(a, b)\n        return string_xor(a, b)\n\n    def xor_and_record(self, a: str, b: str) -> Dict:\n        \"\"\"Computes XOR, and if a repository is available, persists the operation.\n        Returns the saved record dict or a partial dict if no repository.\"\"\"\n        result = self.xor(a, b)\n        \n        record_to_save: Dict = {\"a\": a, \"b\": b, \"result\": result}\n        \n        if self.repository is not None:\n            from .utils import make_uuid, now_iso\n            record_to_save.update({\n                \"id\": make_uuid(),\n                \"timestamp\": now_iso()\n            })\n            try:\n                saved_record = self.repository.save(record_to_save)\n                return saved_record\n            except RepositoryError as e:\n                raise e # Re-raise as per design\n        else:\n            record_to_save[\"id\"] = None\n            record_to_save[\"timestamp\"] = None\n            return record_to_save\n```\n\n```python\n# src/binxor/controller.py\nfrom typing import Optional, Annotated\nimport os\n\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, status, Depends, Header\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n\nfrom .service import BinaryXORService\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, RepositoryError, XORError\nfrom .validator import BinaryValidator\nfrom .repository import XORRepository\n\nclass XOREndpointRequest(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Request body for the POST /xor endpoint.\"\"\"\n    a: str = Field(..., description=\"First binary string\", pattern=\"^[01]*$\")\n    b: str = Field(..., description=\"Second binary string\", pattern=\"^[01]*$\")\n\nclass XOREndpointResponse(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Response body for the POST /xor endpoint.\"\"\"\n    result: str = Field(..., description=\"Result of the bitwise XOR operation\")\n    id: Optional[str] = Field(None, description=\"ID of the persisted operation record\")\n    timestamp: Optional[str] = Field(None, description=\"Timestamp of the operation (ISO 8601)\")\n\napp = FastAPI(\n    title=\"Binary XOR Service\",\n    description=\"Computes bitwise XOR of two binary strings and records operations.\",\n    version=\"0.1.0\"\n)\n\n_validator = BinaryValidator()\n_repository_path = os.environ.get(\"BINXOR_REPO_PATH\", XORRepository.DEFAULT_REPO_PATH)\n_repository = XORRepository(path=_repository_path)\n_xor_service = BinaryXORService(validator=_validator, repository=_repository)\n_api_key = os.environ.get(\"BINXOR_API_KEY\")\n\nclass APIController:\n    \"\"\"HTTP API Controller exposing XOR capabilities.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: BinaryXORService, api_key: Optional[str] = None):\n        self.service = service\n        self.api_key = api_key\n\n    def _api_key_auth(self, x_api_key: Annotated[Optional[str], Header()] = None):\n        \"\"\"Authenticates requests using an optional API key header.\"\"\"\n        if self.api_key:\n            if not x_api_key or x_api_key != self.api_key:\n                raise HTTPException(\n                    status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n                    detail=\"Invalid API Key\"\n                )\n\n    def register_routes(self, app_instance: FastAPI) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Registers the API routes with the provided FastAPI app instance.\"\"\"\n\n        @app_instance.post(\"/xor\", response_model=XOREndpointResponse, status_code=status.HTTP_200_OK)\n        async def compute_endpoint(\n            payload: XOREndpointRequest,\n            auth_status: Annotated[None, Depends(self._api_key_auth)] # Apply authentication if configured\n        ):\n            \"\"\"Computes the bitwise XOR of two binary strings.\n            The operation is persisted if a repository is configured.\"\"\"\n            try:\n                record = self.service.xor_and_record(payload.a, payload.b)\n                return XOREndpointResponse(\n                    result=record[\"result\"],\n                    id=record.get(\"id\"),\n                    timestamp=record.get(\"timestamp\")\n                )\n            except InvalidInputError as e:\n                raise HTTPException(\n                    status_code=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST,\n                    detail=f\"Invalid input: {e}\"\n                )\n            except RepositoryError as e:\n                raise HTTPException(\n                    status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR,\n                    detail=f\"Repository error: {e}\"\n                )\n            except XORError as e:\n                 raise HTTPException(\n                    status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR,\n                    detail=f\"An internal error occurred: {e}\"\n                )\n            except Exception as e:\n                raise HTTPException(\n                    status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR,\n                    detail=f\"An unexpected server error occurred: {e}\"\n                )\n\n_api_controller = APIController(service=_xor_service, api_key=_api_key)\n_api_controller.register_routes(app)\n```\n\n```python\n# src/binxor/cli.py\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nimport os\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nimport json\n\nfrom .service import BinaryXORService\nfrom .validator import BinaryValidator\nfrom .repository import XORRepository\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, RepositoryError, XORError\n\nclass CLI:\n    \"\"\"Command Line Interface for binary XOR operations.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: BinaryXORService):\n        self.service = service\n        self.parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            prog=\"binxor\",\n            description=\"Bitwise XOR utility for binary strings.\"\n        )\n        self._setup_parser()\n\n    def _setup_parser(self):\n        \"\"\"Configures the argument parser with subcommands.\"\"\"\n        subparsers = self.parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", help=\"Available commands\")\n\n        xor_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\"xor\", help=\"Compute XOR of two binary strings\")\n        xor_parser.add_argument(\"--a\", required=True, help=\"First binary string\")\n        xor_parser.add_argument(\"--b\", required=True, help=\"Second binary string\")\n        xor_parser.set_defaults(func=self._handle_xor)\n\n        list_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\"history\", help=\"List recent XOR operations\")\n        list_parser.add_argument(\"--limit\", type=int, default=100, help=\"Number of records to retrieve\")\n        list_parser.add_argument(\"--offset\", type=int, default=0, help=\"Offset for pagination\")\n        list_parser.set_defaults(func=self._handle_history_list)\n\n        get_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\"get-history\", help=\"Retrieve a specific XOR operation by ID\")\n        get_parser.add_argument(\"id\", help=\"UUID of the XOR operation record\")\n        get_parser.set_defaults(func=self._handle_history_get)\n\n    def _handle_xor(self, args) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Handler for the 'xor' command.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            record = self.service.xor_and_record(args.a, args.b)\n            print(record[\"result\"])\n            return 0\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n        except RepositoryError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: Repository problem - {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 3\n        except XORError as e:\n            print(f\"An internal XOR error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n\n    def _handle_history_list(self, args) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Handler for the 'history' command.\"\"\"\n        if self.service.repository is None:\n            print(\"Error: Repository not configured.\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n        try:\n            records = self.service.repository.list(limit=args.limit, offset=args.offset)\n            if not records:\n                print(\"No history records found.\")\n            for record in records:\n                print(f\"ID: {record['id']}, A: {record['a']}, B: {record['b']}, Result: {record['result']}, Time: {record['timestamp']}\")\n            return 0\n        except RepositoryError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: Repository problem - {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 3\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n\n    def _handle_history_get(self, args) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Handler for the 'get-history' command.\"\"\"\n        if self.service.repository is None:\n            print(\"Error: Repository not configured.\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n        try:\n            record = self.service.repository.get(args.id)\n            if record:\n                print(f\"ID: {record['id']}\")\n                print(f\"A: {record['a']}\")\n                print(f\"B: {record['b']}\")\n                print(f\"Result: {record['result']}\")\n                print(f\"Timestamp: {record['timestamp']}\")\n            else:\n                print(f\"No record found with ID: {args.id}\", file=sys.stderr)\n                return 4\n            return 0\n        except RepositoryError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: Repository problem - {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 3\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n\n    def run(self, argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Parses arguments and dispatches to appropriate handler.\n        Returns an exit code.\"\"\"\n        args = self.parser.parse_args(argv)\n        if hasattr(args, 'func'):\n            return args.func(args)\n        else:\n            self.parser.print_help()\n            return 1\n\ndef main(argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Entry point for the binxor CLI.\"\"\"\n    validator = BinaryValidator()\n    repository_path = os.environ.get(\"BINXOR_REPO_PATH\", XORRepository.DEFAULT_REPO_PATH)\n    repository = XORRepository(path=repository_path)\n    service = BinaryXORService(validator=validator, repository=repository)\n\n    cli = CLI(service)\n    return cli.run(argv if argv is not None else sys.argv[1:])\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/11", "solution": "```python\ndef string_xor(a: str, b: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Perform binary XOR on two strings of 1s and 0s.\n    Shorter input is left-padded with '0's to match lengths.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = max(len(a), len(b))\n    a_padded = a.rjust(n, '0')\n    b_padded = b.rjust(n, '0')\n\n    result_chars = []\n    for char_a, char_b in zip(a_padded, b_padded):\n        if char_a != char_b:\n            result_chars.append('1')\n        else:\n            result_chars.append('0')\n    \n    return \"\".join(result_chars)\n```"}
