{"task_id": "HumanEval/35", "solution": "```python\n# src/maxfinder/__init__.py\n\"\"\"Maxfinder package for computing the maximum element in a list.\"\"\"\n\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n\nfrom .max_element_service import MaxElementService\nfrom .in_memory_repository import InMemoryHistoryRepository\nfrom .sqlite_repository import SQLiteHistoryRepository\nfrom .repository import HistoryRepository\nfrom .models import ListInputDTO, MaxResultDTO, HistoryRecord\nfrom .config import Config\nfrom .controller import MaxController\nfrom .cli import run_cli as _run_cli # Internal import for __main__ entry point\nimport sys\n\ndef create_app():\n    \"\"\"Factory function to create the FastAPI application.\"\"\"\n    config = Config.from_env()\n    if config.persist_history:\n        repo = SQLiteHistoryRepository(db_path=config.db_path)\n    else:\n        repo = InMemoryHistoryRepository()\n    service = MaxElementService(repo=repo)\n    return MaxController(service=service, config=config).create_app()\n\ndef main_cli():\n    \"\"\"Entry point for the command-line interface.\"\"\"\n    sys.exit(_run_cli(sys.argv[1:]))\n\n# This package also exposes the MaxElementService directly for programmatic use.\n# Example:\n# from maxfinder import MaxElementService, InMemoryHistoryRepository\n# service = MaxElementService(repo=InMemoryHistoryRepository())\n# result = service.compute_max([1, 5, 2])\n# print(result.value) # 5\n\n# Or, if you want the very bare function (adhering to the original problem statement's constraints\n# for a simple, direct max computation without checks or wrappers for internal use):\nfrom ._bare_max_element import max_element\n```\n\n```python\n# src/maxfinder/config.py\n\"\"\"Configuration management for the MaxFinder application.\"\"\"\n\nimport os\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nclass Config:\n    \"\"\"Application configuration loaded from environment variables or defaults.\"\"\"\n\n    DEFAULT_DB_PATH = \"maxfinder_history.db\"\n    DEFAULT_PERSIST_HISTORY = \"false\" # Use string for env var parsing\n\n    def __init__(self, db_path: str, persist_history: bool, api_key: Optional[str]):\n        \"\"\"Initialize Config with provided values.\"\"\"\n        self.db_path = db_path\n        self.persist_history = persist_history\n        self.api_key = api_key\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def from_env() -> 'Config':\n        \"\"\"Load configuration from environment variables.\"\"\"\n        db_path = os.getenv(\"MAXFINDER_DB_PATH\", Config.DEFAULT_DB_PATH)\n        persist_history_str = os.getenv(\"MAXFINDER_PERSIST_HISTORY\", Config.DEFAULT_PERSIST_HISTORY).lower()\n        persist_history = persist_history_str in ('true', '1', 't', 'y')\n        api_key = os.getenv(\"MAXFINDER_API_KEY\")\n        return Config(db_path=db_path, persist_history=persist_history, api_key=api_key)\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/maxfinder/models.py\n\"\"\"Data Transfer Objects (DTOs) and domain models for MaxFinder.\"\"\"\n\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom typing import Any, List, Optional\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field # For FastAPI request/response validation\n\nclass ListInputDTO(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"DTO for input list of items.\"\"\"\n    items: List[Any] = Field(..., description=\"List of comparable items to find the maximum from.\")\n\nclass MaxResultDTO(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"DTO for the result of a maximum element computation.\"\"\"\n    value: Any = Field(..., description=\"The maximum element found in the input list.\")\n    input_len: int = Field(..., description=\"The number of elements in the input list.\")\n    computed_at: datetime = Field(default_factory=datetime.utcnow, description=\"Timestamp of when the maximum was computed (UTC).\")\n\nclass HistoryRecord(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Model for a persisted invocation history record.\"\"\"\n    id: Optional[int] = Field(None, description=\"Unique identifier for the history record.\")\n    input_json: str = Field(..., description=\"JSON string representation of the input list.\")\n    result_json: str = Field(..., description=\"JSON string representation of the computed maximum result.\")\n    created_at: datetime = Field(default_factory=datetime.utcnow, description=\"Timestamp of when the record was created (UTC).\")\n\nHISTORY_TABLE = \"history\"\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/maxfinder/exceptions.py\n\"\"\"Custom exceptions for the MaxFinder application.\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nclass ValidationError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for invalid input data.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\nclass PersistenceError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for errors during history persistence operations.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str, original_exception: Optional[Exception] = None):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n        self.original_exception = original_exception\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/maxfinder/logger.py\n\"\"\"Configures and provides a shared logger instance for the MaxFinder application.\"\"\"\n\nimport logging\nimport os\n\ndef setup_logger():\n    \"\"\"Set up and return a configured logger.\"\"\"\n    logger = logging.getLogger(\"maxfinder\")\n    if not logger.handlers: # Prevent adding multiple handlers if setup is called multiple times\n        handler = logging.StreamHandler()\n        formatter = logging.Formatter('%(asctime)s - %(name)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s')\n        handler.setFormatter(formatter)\n        logger.addHandler(handler)\n        log_level = os.getenv(\"MAXFINDER_LOG_LEVEL\", \"INFO\").upper()\n        logger.setLevel(log_level)\n    return logger\n\nlogger = setup_logger()\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/maxfinder/utils.py\n\"\"\"Utility functions for parsing, validation, and JSON serialization.\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nfrom typing import Any, List, Union\nfrom collections.abc import Iterable\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\nfrom .logger import logger\n\ndef parse_list_input(raw: Union[str, List[Any]]) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Parses a raw input (string or list) into a list of Python values.\n    Accepts CSV strings, JSON array strings, or a direct list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if isinstance(raw, list):\n        return raw\n    \n    if isinstance(raw, str):\n        try:\n            # Try parsing as JSON array first\n            parsed_json = json.loads(raw)\n            if isinstance(parsed_json, list):\n                return parsed_json\n            raise ValidationError(\"JSON input must be a list.\")\n        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n            # Fallback to CSV parsing\n            if not raw.strip(): # Check for empty string after JSON attempt\n                raise ValidationError(\"Input cannot be an empty string if not a valid JSON array.\")\n            return [item.strip() for item in raw.split(',')]\n    \n    raise ValidationError(f\"Unsupported input type: {type(raw)}. Expected string or list.\")\n\ndef is_iterable(obj: Any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if an object is iterable but not a string.\"\"\"\n    return isinstance(obj, Iterable) and not isinstance(obj, (str, bytes))\n\ndef to_json(obj: Any) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Safely serializes an object to a JSON string, handling non-serializable types.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return json.dumps(obj)\n    except TypeError:\n        # Fallback for non-serializable objects (e.g., custom classes not handled by default)\n        # Representation might be less useful but ensures string output.\n        logger.warning(f\"Object of type {type(obj)} not directly JSON serializable. Using str().\")\n        return json.dumps(str(obj))\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/maxfinder/_bare_max_element.py\n# This file implements the original `max_element` function conforming strictly\n# to its specific constraints (no checks, no helpers, bare function).\n# This is an internal detail, used by MaxElementService._compute.\n\ndef max_element(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return maximum element in the list, assuming non-empty and comparable elements.\n    This function performs the core computation without any input validation or error handling,\n    trusting that the caller provides valid inputs as per its strict definition.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_max = l[0]\n    for item in l:\n        if item > current_max:\n            current_max = item\n    return current_max\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/maxfinder/max_element_service.py\n\"\"\"Service layer for computing the maximum element and managing history.\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Any, List, Optional\nfrom datetime import datetime\nimport json\n\nfrom .models import MaxResultDTO, HistoryRecord\nfrom .repository import HistoryRepository\nfrom .in_memory_repository import InMemoryHistoryRepository # Default if no repo provided\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError, PersistenceError\nfrom .utils import is_iterable, to_json\nfrom .logger import logger\nfrom ._bare_max_element import max_element as _bare_max_element # Import the core computation\n\nclass MaxElementService:\n    \"\"\"\n    Orchestrates validation, computes the maximum element, and optionally persists history.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, repo: Optional[HistoryRepository] = None):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes the MaxElementService with an optional history repository.\n        If no repository is provided, an InMemoryHistoryRepository is used.\n        \"\"\"\n        self._repo: HistoryRepository = repo if repo is not None else InMemoryHistoryRepository()\n\n    def compute_max(self, items: List[Any]) -> MaxResultDTO:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes the maximum element in a list after validation, then records history.\n        Raises ValidationError for invalid inputs.\n        \"\"\"\n        self._validate_input(items)\n\n        try:\n            # The core computation logic, adhering to the \"bare function\" constraints.\n            # This method (_bare_max_element) assumes valid input (non-empty, comparable).\n            max_val = self._compute(items)\n        except TypeError as e:\n            # Catch Python's native TypeError for incomparable types\n            raise ValidationError(f\"Elements in list are not comparable: {e}\") from e\n        except Exception as e:\n            # Catch other unexpected errors during computation\n            logger.error(f\"Unexpected error during max computation: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n            raise\n\n        result_dto = MaxResultDTO(value=max_val, input_len=len(items))\n        self._record_history(items, result_dto)\n        return result_dto\n\n    def _validate_input(self, items: List[Any]):\n        \"\"\"Validates the input list for computation.\"\"\"\n        if not is_iterable(items):\n            raise ValidationError(\"Input must be a list or iterable.\")\n        if not items:\n            raise ValidationError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n\n    def _compute(self, items: List[Any]) -> Any:\n        \"\"\"\n        Core computation of the maximum element.\n        This method uses the _bare_max_element function, which assumes valid input\n        (non-empty, comparable) and performs the direct max finding logic.\n        \"\"\"\n        return _bare_max_element(items)\n\n    def _record_history(self, input_items: List[Any], result: MaxResultDTO):\n        \"\"\"Records the computation history in the repository (best-effort).\"\"\"\n        if self._repo:\n            try:\n                input_json = to_json(input_items)\n                result_json = to_json(result.value) # Only store the value, not the whole DTO\n                record = HistoryRecord(\n                    id=None,\n                    input_json=input_json,\n                    result_json=result_json,\n                    created_at=result.computed_at\n                )\n                self._repo.save(record)\n            except PersistenceError as e:\n                logger.error(f\"Failed to persist history: {e.message}\", exc_info=True)\n            except Exception as e:\n                logger.error(f\"Unexpected error during history recording: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n        else:\n            logger.debug(\"History repository not configured, skipping history persistence.\")\n    \n    def get_history(self) -> List[HistoryRecord]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves all history records from the repository.\"\"\"\n        if self._repo:\n            try:\n                return self._repo.get_all()\n            except PersistenceError as e:\n                logger.error(f\"Failed to retrieve history: {e.message}\", exc_info=True)\n                raise\n            except Exception as e:\n                logger.error(f\"Unexpected error during history retrieval: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n                raise\n        return []\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/maxfinder/repository.py\n\"\"\"Abstract base class for history repositories.\"\"\"\n\nfrom abc import ABC, abstractmethod\nfrom typing import List\n\nfrom .models import HistoryRecord\n\nclass HistoryRepository(ABC):\n    \"\"\"Abstract base class defining the contract for history persistence.\"\"\"\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    def save(self, record: HistoryRecord) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Saves a history record.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    def get_all(self) -> List[HistoryRecord]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves all history records.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/maxfinder/in_memory_repository.py\n\"\"\"In-memory implementation of the HistoryRepository.\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any\nfrom threading import Lock\n\nfrom .repository import HistoryRepository\nfrom .models import HistoryRecord\n\nclass InMemoryHistoryRepository(HistoryRepository):\n    \"\"\"\n    An in-memory implementation of HistoryRepository, primarily for testing and ephemeral use.\n    Not thread-safe for write operations without external locking.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the in-memory store.\"\"\"\n        self._store: List[HistoryRecord] = []\n        self._next_id = 1\n        self._lock = Lock() # Ensure thread-safe ID generation and append\n\n    def save(self, record: HistoryRecord) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Saves a history record to the in-memory store.\"\"\"\n        with self._lock:\n            record.id = self._next_id\n            self._next_id += 1\n            self._store.append(record)\n\n    def get_all(self) -> List[HistoryRecord]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves all history records from the in-memory store.\"\"\"\n        # Return a copy to prevent external modification\n        return sorted(self._store, key=lambda x: x.created_at, reverse=True)\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/maxfinder/sqlite_repository.py\n\"\"\"SQLite-backed implementation of the HistoryRepository.\"\"\"\n\nimport sqlite3\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\nfrom .repository import HistoryRepository\nfrom .models import HistoryRecord, HISTORY_TABLE\nfrom .exceptions import PersistenceError\nfrom .logger import logger\n\nclass SQLiteHistoryRepository(HistoryRepository):\n    \"\"\"\n    SQLite-backed implementation of the HistoryRepository.\n    Manages database connection and schema migration.\n    \"\"\"\n    CREATE_TABLE_SQL = f\"\"\"\n    CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS {HISTORY_TABLE} (\n        id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n        input_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n        result_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n        created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n    );\n    \"\"\"\n    CREATE_INDEX_SQL = f\"CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_{HISTORY_TABLE}_created_at ON {HISTORY_TABLE}(created_at);\"\n\n    def __init__(self, db_path: str):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes the SQLite repository with the given database path.\n        Automatically connects and performs migrations.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.db_path = db_path\n        self._conn: Optional[sqlite3.Connection] = None\n        self._connect()\n        self._migrate()\n\n    def _connect(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Establishes a connection to the SQLite database.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            self._conn = sqlite3.connect(self.db_path, check_same_thread=False) # Allow multi-thread for FastAPI\n            self._conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row # Access columns by name\n            logger.info(f\"Connected to SQLite database: {self.db_path}\")\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Failed to connect to SQLite database {self.db_path}\", original_exception=e) from e\n\n    def _get_connection(self) -> sqlite3.Connection:\n        \"\"\"Returns the current database connection, reconnecting if necessary.\"\"\"\n        if self._conn is None:\n            self._connect()\n        return self._conn # type: ignore\n\n    def _migrate(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Applies necessary database schema migrations.\"\"\"\n        conn = self._get_connection()\n        try:\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(self.CREATE_TABLE_SQL)\n            cursor.execute(self.CREATE_INDEX_SQL)\n            conn.commit()\n            logger.info(\"SQLite database schema migrated successfully.\")\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            conn.rollback()\n            raise PersistenceError(\"Failed to migrate SQLite database schema\", original_exception=e) from e\n\n    def save(self, record: HistoryRecord) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Saves a history record to the SQLite database.\"\"\"\n        conn = self._get_connection()\n        try:\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(\n                f\"INSERT INTO {HISTORY_TABLE} (input_json, result_json, created_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?)\",\n                (record.input_json, record.result_json, record.created_at.isoformat())\n            )\n            conn.commit()\n            record.id = cursor.lastrowid # Update record with generated ID\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            conn.rollback()\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Failed to save history record: {record}\", original_exception=e) from e\n\n    def get_all(self) -> List[HistoryRecord]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves all history records from the SQLite database, ordered by creation date (desc).\"\"\"\n        conn = self._get_connection()\n        try:\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(f\"SELECT id, input_json, result_json, created_at FROM {HISTORY_TABLE} ORDER BY created_at DESC\")\n            rows = cursor.fetchall()\n            return [\n                HistoryRecord(\n                    id=row['id'],\n                    input_json=row['input_json'],\n                    result_json=row['result_json'],\n                    created_at=datetime.fromisoformat(row['created_at'])\n                )\n                for row in rows\n            ]\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            raise PersistenceError(\"Failed to retrieve history records\", original_exception=e) from e\n\n    def close(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Closes the database connection.\"\"\"\n        if self._conn:\n            self._conn.close()\n            self._conn = None\n            logger.info(f\"Closed SQLite database connection for {self.db_path}\")\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/maxfinder/controller.py\n\"\"\"HTTP API controllers using FastAPI for MaxFinder.\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Optional, Any\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, status, Request, Response, Depends\nfrom fastapi.responses import JSONResponse\nfrom pydantic import ValidationError as PydanticValidationError # Alias to avoid clash\nfrom functools import wraps\n\nfrom .max_element_service import MaxElementService\nfrom .models import ListInputDTO, MaxResultDTO, HistoryRecord\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError, PersistenceError\nfrom .config import Config\nfrom .logger import logger\nfrom .utils import parse_list_input\n\ndef get_api_key_header(request: Request, config: Config) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Dependency to check for API key if configured.\"\"\"\n    if not config.api_key:\n        return \"\" # No API key required\n    \n    api_key_header = request.headers.get(\"X-API-KEY\")\n    if api_key_header is None:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n            detail=\"X-API-KEY header missing\"\n        )\n    if api_key_header != config.api_key:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n            detail=\"Invalid API Key\"\n        )\n    return api_key_header\n\nclass MaxController:\n    \"\"\"\n    Handles HTTP requests for maximum element computation and history retrieval.\n    Integrates with FastAPI.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: MaxElementService, config: Config):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the controller with a MaxElementService and Config.\"\"\"\n        self._service = service\n        self._config = config\n        self._app = FastAPI(\n            title=\"MaxFinder Service\",\n            description=\"API for computing the maximum element in a list and managing history.\",\n            version=self._config.__version__ if hasattr(self._config, '__version__') else \"0.1.0\"\n        )\n        self._register_routes()\n        self._register_exception_handlers()\n\n    def create_app(self) -> FastAPI:\n        \"\"\"Returns the configured FastAPI application instance.\"\"\"\n        return self._app\n\n    def _register_routes(self):\n        \"\"\"Registers the API endpoints.\"\"\"\n        self._app.post(\"/max\", response_model=MaxResultDTO)(self.post_max)\n        self._app.get(\"/history\", response_model=List[HistoryRecord])(self.get_history)\n        # Add root path for basic health check/info\n        self._app.get(\"/\")(self.read_root)\n\n    def _register_exception_handlers(self):\n        \"\"\"Registers custom exception handlers for FastAPI.\"\"\"\n\n        @self._app.exception_handler(ValidationError)\n        async def validation_error_handler(request: Request, exc: ValidationError):\n            logger.warning(f\"Client input validation error: {exc.message}\")\n            return JSONResponse(\n                status_code=status.HTTP_422_UNPROCESSABLE_ENTITY,\n                content={\"detail\": [{\"msg\": exc.message, \"type\": \"validation_error\"}]}\n            )\n        \n        @self._app.exception_handler(PydanticValidationError)\n        async def pydantic_validation_error_handler(request: Request, exc: PydanticValidationError):\n            logger.warning(f\"Pydantic validation error: {exc.errors()}\")\n            return JSONResponse(\n                status_code=status.HTTP_422_UNPROCESSABLE_ENTITY,\n                content={\"detail\": exc.errors()}\n            )\n\n        @self._app.exception_handler(PersistenceError)\n        async def persistence_error_handler(request: Request, exc: PersistenceError):\n            logger.error(f\"Persistence error: {exc.message}\", exc_info=True)\n            return JSONResponse(\n                status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR,\n                content={\"detail\": \"A server error occurred during data persistence. Please try again later.\"}\n            )\n\n        @self._app.exception_handler(Exception)\n        async def generic_exception_handler(request: Request, exc: Exception):\n            logger.exception(f\"An unhandled server error occurred: {exc}\")\n            return JSONResponse(\n                status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR,\n                content={\"detail\": \"An unexpected server error occurred.\"}\n            )\n    \n    async def read_root(self):\n        \"\"\"Root endpoint for basic service info.\"\"\"\n        return {\"message\": \"MaxFinder Service is running!\", \"version\": self._app.version}\n\n    async def post_max(\n        self, \n        list_input_dto: ListInputDTO,\n        api_key: str = Depends(get_api_key_header) # Dependency injection for API key check\n    ) -> MaxResultDTO:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes the maximum element of a given list.\n        Expects a JSON body like: `{ \"items\": [1, 2, 3] }`\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            # Pydantic (ListInputDTO) handles initial JSON parsing and type checks.\n            # Convert to plain list for service logic.\n            items_for_service = list_input_dto.items\n            result = self._service.compute_max(items_for_service)\n            return result\n        except ValidationError as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_422_UNPROCESSABLE_ENTITY, detail=e.message)\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.exception(f\"Unhandled error in post_max: {e}\")\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, detail=\"An unexpected server error occurred.\")\n\n    async def get_history(\n        self,\n        limit: int = 100,\n        api_key: str = Depends(get_api_key_header) # Dependency injection for API key check\n    ) -> List[HistoryRecord]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Retrieves the invocation history, optionally limited by count.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            all_records = self._service.get_history()\n            # Apply limit if requested. History is already sorted by date descending from repository.\n            return all_records[:limit]\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.exception(f\"Unhandled error in get_history: {e}\")\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, detail=\"Failed to retrieve history.\")\n\n# Note: The `app` instance needs to be created at the module level for Uvicorn.\n# For local development or production deployment with Uvicorn, you would typically do:\n# from maxfinder import create_app\n# app = create_app()\n# and then run `uvicorn your_module_name:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000`\n# or `uvicorn maxfinder.controller:app --factory`\n# For this specific design, create_app is a factory method on MaxController.\n# To make it accessible for uvicorn, we can instantiate it here\n_config = Config.from_env()\n_repo = None\nif _config.persist_history:\n    _repo = SQLiteHistoryRepository(db_path=_config.db_path)\nelse:\n    _repo = InMemoryHistoryRepository()\n_service = MaxElementService(repo=_repo)\napp = MaxController(service=_service, config=_config).create_app()\n```\n\n```python\n# src/maxfinder/cli.py\n\"\"\"Command-line interface for the MaxFinder application.\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nfrom .max_element_service import MaxElementService\nfrom .in_memory_repository import InMemoryHistoryRepository\nfrom .sqlite_repository import SQLiteHistoryRepository\nfrom .config import Config\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\nfrom .utils import parse_list_input\nfrom .logger import logger\n\nclass CLI:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates the command-line interface logic.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, service: MaxElementService):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the CLI with a MaxElementService.\"\"\"\n        self._service = service\n\n    def execute(self, items_raw: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Executes the max finding operation for the CLI.\n        Returns 0 on success, non-zero on error.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            items = parse_list_input(items_raw)\n            result = self._service.compute_max(items)\n            print(f\"Maximum element: {result.value}\")\n            return 0\n        except ValidationError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: {e.message}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.error(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n            print(\"An unexpected error occurred. Check logs for details.\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n\ndef run_cli(argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Main entry point for the command-line interface script.\n    Parses arguments and delegates to the CLI class.\n    \"\"\"\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"Compute the maximum element of a list.\",\n        formatter_class=argparse.ArgumentDefaultsHelpFormatter\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"items\",\n        type=str,\n        help=\"Input list as a comma-separated string (e.g., '1,2,3') or a JSON array string (e.g., '[\\\"a\\\",\\\"b\\\"]').\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--db-path\",\n        type=str,\n        default=Config.DEFAULT_DB_PATH,\n        help=\"Path to the SQLite database file for history persistence.\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--persist-history\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        default=False,\n        help=\"Enable persistence of invocation history to SQLite.\"\n    )\n\n    args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n    repo = None\n    if args.persist_history:\n        try:\n            repo = SQLiteHistoryRepository(db_path=args.db_path)\n            logger.info(f\"Using SQLite for history persistence at {args.db_path}\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Failed to initialize SQLite repository: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n            print(f\"Warning: Failed to initialize SQLite repository. History will not be persisted. Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            repo = InMemoryHistoryRepository() # Fallback\n    else:\n        repo = InMemoryHistoryRepository()\n        logger.info(\"Using in-memory repository for history (not persisted).\")\n\n    service = MaxElementService(repo=repo)\n    cli = CLI(service=service)\n    return cli.execute(args.items)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(run_cli())\n\n```\n\n```toml\n# pyproject.toml\n[project]\nname = \"maxfinder\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A reliable library and service to compute the maximum element of a list.\"\nauthors = [\n    { name = \"Your Name\", email = \"your.email@example.com\" }\n]\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.9\"\nkeywords = [\"max\", \"maximum\", \"list\", \"api\", \"cli\", \"fastapi\"]\nclassifiers = [\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n    \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\",\n    \"Operating System :: OS Independent\",\n]\n\ndependencies = [\n    \"pydantic>=2.0.0\", # For DTO validation and FastAPI integration\n    \"fastapi[all]>=0.111.0\", # For HTTP API, includes uvicorn, standard JSON handling\n]\n\n[project.optional-dependencies]\ndev = [\n    \"pytest>=8.0.0\",\n    \"pytest-cov>=5.0.0\",\n    \"httpx>=0.27.0\", # For testing FastAPI endpoints\n]\n\n[project.scripts]\nmaxfinder-cli = \"maxfinder.cli:run_cli\"\nmaxfinder-api = \"uvicorn maxfinder.controller:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[tool.setuptools]\npackages = [\"maxfinder\"]\n\n[tool.setuptools.package-dir]\nmaxfinder = \"src/maxfinder\"\n\n[tool.setuptools.packages.find]\nwhere = [\"src\"]\n\n```\n\n```markdown\n# README.md\n# MaxFinder\n\nMaxFinder is a Python library and service designed to reliably compute the maximum element of a list of comparable values. It offers multiple usage surfaces including a programmatic API, a command-line interface (CLI), and an HTTP API for remote invocation. It also records invocation history for auditing and debugging.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Programmatic API**: A Python service class for direct integration into other Python projects.\n- **CLI**: A command-line tool to compute maxima from scripts or the terminal.\n- **HTTP API**: A RESTful endpoint for remote computation using JSON over HTTP.\n- **Invocation History**: Persists request inputs, results, and timestamps (in-memory or SQLite).\n- **Lightweight**: Minimal dependencies, with FastAPI and SQLite as optional features.\n\n## Installation\n\n### Using pip (Recommended)\n\nFirst, ensure you have Python 3.9+ installed.\n\n```bash\n# Install the core library\npip install maxfinder\n\n# To include FastAPI and Uvicorn for the HTTP API:\npip install maxfinder[all]\n```\n\n### From Source\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/yourusername/maxfinder.git # Replace with actual repo URL\ncd maxfinder\npip install .\n\n# If you want to run the HTTP API\npip install .[all]\n\n# For development (including testing dependencies)\npip install .[dev]\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### 1. Programmatic API\n\nYou can use the `MaxElementService` directly in your Python applications.\n\n```python\nfrom maxfinder import MaxElementService, InMemoryHistoryRepository, SQLiteHistoryRepository\nfrom maxfinder.exceptions import ValidationError\n\n# Using an in-memory repository (default if not specified)\n# This is useful for tests or temporary computations without persistence.\nin_memory_repo = InMemoryHistoryRepository()\nservice_in_memory = MaxElementService(repo=in_memory_repo)\n\ntry:\n    result = service_in_memory.compute_max([10, 5, 20, 3])\n    print(f\"Max element (in-memory): {result.value}\") # Output: 20\n    print(f\"Input length: {result.input_len}\")\n    \n    # Retrieve history\n    history = service_in_memory.get_history()\n    print(f\"History records (in-memory): {len(history)}\")\n\nexcept ValidationError as e:\n    print(f\"Input error: {e.message}\")\n\n# Using a SQLite repository for persistent history\n# The database file 'my_max_history.db' will be created/used.\nsqlite_repo = SQLiteHistoryRepository(db_path=\"my_max_history.db\")\nservice_sqlite = MaxElementService(repo=sqlite_repo)\n\ntry:\n    result_db = service_sqlite.compute_max([100, -50, 250])\n    print(f\"Max element (SQLite): {result_db.value}\") # Output: 250\n\n    # Retrieve history from SQLite\n    history_db = service_sqlite.get_history()\n    print(f\"History records (SQLite): {len(history_db)}\")\n\nexcept ValidationError as e:\n    print(f\"Input error: {e.message}\")\nfinally:\n    sqlite_repo.close() # Important to close SQLite connection gracefully\n```\n\n### 2. Command-Line Interface (CLI)\n\nThe CLI tool `maxfinder-cli` allows you to compute maxima directly from your terminal.\n\n```bash\n# Basic usage with comma-separated values\nmaxfinder-cli \"10,20,5,30\"\n# Output: Maximum element: 30\n\n# Using JSON array input (useful for mixed types or strings)\nmaxfinder-cli '[\"apple\", \"banana\", \"kiwi\"]'\n# Output: Maximum element: kiwi\n\nmaxfinder-cli '[1, 5, \"a\"]' # Incomparable types\n# Output: Error: Elements in list are not comparable: '>' not supported between instances of 'int' and 'str'\n\n# Empty list\nmaxfinder-cli '[]'\n# Output: Error: Input list cannot be empty\n\n# Enable history persistence to a SQLite database\nmaxfinder-cli \"1,2,3\" --persist-history --db-path my_cli_history.db\n# Output: Maximum element: 3\n# A 'my_cli_history.db' file will be created/updated with the record.\n\n# Get help\nmaxfinder-cli --help\n```\n\n### 3. HTTP API\n\nThe HTTP API allows remote clients to interact with the MaxFinder service.\nYou need to install with the `[all]` extra to get `fastapi` and `uvicorn`.\n\n```bash\npip install maxfinder[all]\n```\n\nTo run the API service:\n\n```bash\nmaxfinder-api\n```\nBy default, this will start the service on `http://127.0.0.1:8000`.\n\n#### Endpoints\n\n##### `POST /max`\n\nComputes the maximum element of a list.\n\n- **Request Body**:\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"items\": [1, 5, 2, 8]\n  }\n  ```\n  or (string will be parsed internally)\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"items\": \"1,5,2,8\"\n  }\n  ```\n- **Response `200 OK`**:\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"value\": 8,\n    \"input_len\": 4,\n    \"computed_at\": \"2023-10-27T10:30:00.123456\"\n  }\n  ```\n- **Error Responses**:\n  - `422 Unprocessable Entity`: For invalid input (e.g., empty list, incomparable types).\n  - `401 Unauthorized`: If `MAXFINDER_API_KEY` is set and `X-API-KEY` header is missing or incorrect.\n  - `500 Internal Server Error`: For unexpected server issues (e.g., persistence failures).\n\nExample using `curl`:\n\n```bash\n# Basic request\ncurl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/max \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\"items\": [10, 30, 20]}'\n\n# Request with API Key (if configured via MAXFINDER_API_KEY environment variable)\n# export MAXFINDER_API_KEY=\"my-secret-key\"\n# curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/max \\\n#      -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n#      -H \"X-API-KEY: my-secret-key\" \\\n#      -d '{\"items\": [10, 30, 20]}'\n```\n\n##### `GET /history`\n\nRetrieves the persisted invocation history.\n\n- **Query Parameters**:\n  - `limit` (optional, int): Maximum number of history records to return (default: 100).\n- **Response `200 OK`**:\n  ```json\n  [\n    {\n      \"id\": 1,\n      \"input_json\": \"[1, 5, 2]\",\n      \"result_json\": \"5\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2023-10-27T10:00:00.000000\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 2,\n      \"input_json\": \"[10, 30, 20]\",\n      \"result_json\": \"30\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2023-10-27T10:01:00.000000\"\n    }\n  ]\n  ```\n- **Error Responses**:\n  - `401 Unauthorized`: If `MAXFINDER_API_KEY` is set and `X-API-KEY` header is missing or incorrect.\n  - `500 Internal Server Error`: For unexpected server issues (e.g., database errors).\n\nExample using `curl`:\n\n```bash\ncurl http://127.0.0.1:8000/history?limit=5\n```\n\n### Configuration\n\nMaxFinder can be configured using environment variables:\n\n- `MAXFINDER_DB_PATH`: Path to the SQLite database file (default: `maxfinder_history.db`).\n- `MAXFINDER_PERSIST_HISTORY`: Set to `true` or `1` to enable SQLite persistence (default: `false`, uses in-memory).\n- `MAXFINDER_API_KEY`: If set, an `X-API-KEY` header with this value will be required for API endpoints.\n- `MAXFINDER_LOG_LEVEL`: Set the logging level (e.g., `DEBUG`, `INFO`, `WARNING`, `ERROR`) (default: `INFO`).\n\n## Development\n\n### Running Tests\n\nTo run the unit and integration tests (after installing `.[dev]`):\n\n```bash\npytest\n```\n\n### Building the Package\n\n```bash\npython -m build\n```\n\nThis will create distribution files in the `dist/` directory.\n```"}
