{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "def median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    The list is sorted, and the median is calculated based on its length.\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_l)\n    mid = n // 2\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # Odd length list, return the middle element.\n        val = sorted_l[mid]\n        return int(val) if float(val).is_integer() else val\n    else:\n        # Even length list, return the average of the two middle elements.\n        a, b = sorted_l[mid - 1], sorted_l[mid]\n        return (a + b) / 2.0"}
