{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "def encode_shift(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Shifts every lowercase letter by +5 in the ASCII alphabet, preserving other characters.\n    \"\"\"\n    offset = 5\n    encoded_chars = []\n    for ch in s:\n        if 'a' <= ch <= 'z':\n            shifted_char = chr(((ord(ch) - ord('a') + offset) % 26) + ord('a'))\n            encoded_chars.append(shifted_char)\n        else:\n            encoded_chars.append(ch)\n    return \"\".join(encoded_chars)\n\n\ndef decode_shift(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses the encode_shift operation, shifting lowercase letters by -5.\n    \"\"\"\n    offset = 5\n    reverse_offset = (26 - offset) % 26\n    decoded_chars = []\n    for ch in s:\n        if 'a' <= ch <= 'z':\n            shifted_char = chr(((ord(ch) - ord('a') + reverse_offset) % 26) + ord('a'))\n            decoded_chars.append(shifted_char)\n        else:\n            decoded_chars.append(ch)\n    return \"\".join(decoded_chars)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "```python\n# filename: pyproject.toml\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[project]\nname = \"shift-cipher\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A Python library and CLI for Caesar-style shift cipher.\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.9\"\nlicense = { text = \"MIT\" }\nkeywords = [\"cipher\", \"shift\", \"caesar\", \"cli\", \"library\"]\nauthors = [\n  { name = \"Your Name\", email = \"your.email@example.com\" },\n]\nclassifiers = [\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n    \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\",\n    \"Operating System :: OS Independent\",\n    \"Development Status :: 3 - Alpha\",\n    \"Intended Audience :: Developers\",\n    \"Topic :: Security :: Cryptography\",\n]\n\n[project.urls]\nHomepage = \"https://github.com/your-username/shift-cipher\"\n\"Bug Tracker\" = \"https://github.com/your-username/shift-cipher/issues\"\n\n[project.scripts]\nshift-cipher = \"shift_cipher.app:main\"\n\n[project.optional-dependencies]\ndev = [\"pytest>=7.0\"]\n\n```python\n# filename: README.md\n# Shift Cipher Library\n\nA Python library and CLI tool for encoding and decoding lowercase alphabetic strings using a Caesar-style shift of 5 positions.\n\n## Features\n\n-   Encode and decode strings programmatically.\n-   CLI for file-based or direct text input/output.\n-   Built with testability and modularity in mind.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install shift-cipher\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Command Line Interface\n\nEncode text directly:\n```bash\nshift-cipher encode --text \"hello\"\n```\nOutput: `mjqqt`\n\nDecode text from a file and save to another file:\n```bash\necho \"mjqqt\" > input.txt\nshift-cipher decode --file input.txt --output decoded.txt\ncat decoded.txt\n```\nOutput: `hello`\n\nGet help:\n```bash\nshift-cipher --help\nshift-cipher encode --help\n```\n\n### Programmatic API\n\n```python\nfrom shift_cipher.app import main\nfrom shift_cipher.services.cipher_service import CipherService\nfrom shift_cipher.services.encoder import EncoderService\nfrom shift_cipher.services.decoder import DecoderService\nfrom shift_cipher.repositories.file_repository import FileRepository\nfrom shift_cipher.models import CipherRequest, CipherResult\nfrom shift_cipher.config import Config\n\n# Initialize components\nconfig = Config()\nfile_repo = FileRepository(encoding=config.default_encoding)\nencoder = EncoderService(shift=config.max_shift)\ndecoder = DecoderService(shift=config.max_shift)\ncipher_service = CipherService(encoder=encoder, decoder=decoder, repo=file_repo)\n\n# Encode a string\nrequest_encode = CipherRequest(input_text=\"hello\", mode=\"encode\")\nresult_encode: CipherResult = cipher_service.encode(request_encode)\nprint(f\"Encoded: {result_encode.result_text}\") # Output: mjqqt\n\n# Decode a string\nrequest_decode = CipherRequest(input_text=\"mjqqt\", mode=\"decode\")\nresult_decode: CipherResult = cipher_service.decode(request_decode)\nprint(f\"Decoded: {result_decode.result_text}\") # Output: hello\n\n# You can also use the main entry point as a function:\n# import sys\n# sys.exit(main(['encode', '--text', 'test']))\n```\n\n## Development\n\nClone the repository:\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/your-username/shift-cipher.git\ncd shift-cipher\n```\n\nInstall development dependencies:\n```bash\npip install -e .[dev]\n```\n\nRun tests (requires `pytest`):\n```bash\npytest\n```\n\n## Contributing\n\nPlease report issues or suggest improvements on the GitHub repository.\n\n## License\n\nThis project is licensed under the MIT License.\n```python\n# filename: src/shift_cipher/__init__.py\nfrom .app import main\nfrom .config import Config\nfrom .exceptions import ShiftCipherError, ValidationError, FileRepositoryError\nfrom .models import CipherRequest, CipherResult\nfrom .services.encoder import EncoderService\nfrom .services.decoder import DecoderService\nfrom .services.cipher_service import CipherService\nfrom .repositories.file_repository import FileRepository\nfrom .controllers.cli_controller import CLIController\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"main\",\n    \"Config\",\n    \"ShiftCipherError\",\n    \"ValidationError\",\n    \"FileRepositoryError\",\n    \"CipherRequest\",\n    \"CipherResult\",\n    \"EncoderService\",\n    \"DecoderService\",\n    \"CipherService\",\n    \"FileRepository\",\n    \"CLIController\",\n]\n\n```python\n# filename: src/shift_cipher/config.py\nclass Config:\n    \"\"\"Central configuration constants for the shift cipher application.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, max_shift: int = 5, default_encoding: str = \"utf-8\", cli_name: str = \"shift-cipher\"):\n        self.max_shift = max_shift\n        self.default_encoding = default_encoding\n        self.cli_name = cli_name\n\n```python\n# filename: src/shift_cipher/exceptions.py\nclass ShiftCipherError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for all shift cipher related errors.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(self.message)\n\n\nclass ValidationError(ShiftCipherError):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for invalid input data.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\nclass FileRepositoryError(ShiftCipherError):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for file input/output errors.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n```python\n# filename: src/shift_cipher/models.py\nfrom typing import Optional\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass CipherRequest:\n    \"\"\"DTO for encapsulating cipher request parameters.\"\"\"\n    input_text: str\n    mode: str  # \"encode\" or \"decode\"\n    output_path: Optional[str] = None\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass CipherResult:\n    \"\"\"DTO for encapsulating cipher operation results.\"\"\"\n    result_text: str\n    input_length: int\n    mode: str\n\n```python\n# filename: src/shift_cipher/utils/validation.py\nimport re\n\n\ndef validate_lowercase_alpha(s: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Returns True if the string is non-empty and contains only lowercase a-z characters.\"\"\"\n    return bool(s) and re.fullmatch(r'[a-z]+', s) is not None\n\n\ndef sanitize_input(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Strips leading/trailing whitespace from the input string.\"\"\"\n    return s.strip()\n\n```python\n# filename: src/shift_cipher/services/encoder.py\nclass EncoderService:\n    \"\"\"Handles the low-level encoding operation by shifting characters forward.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, shift: int = 5):\n        self._shift = shift\n\n    def encode(self, text: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Encodes a lowercase alphabetic string by shifting each character.\"\"\"\n        return \"\".join(\n            chr(((ord(ch) - ord(\"a\") + self._shift) % 26) + ord(\"a\"))\n            for ch in text\n        )\n\n```python\n# filename: src/shift_cipher/services/decoder.py\nclass DecoderService:\n    \"\"\"Handles the low-level decoding operation by shifting characters backward.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, shift: int = 5):\n        self._shift = shift\n\n    def decode(self, text: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Decodes a lowercase alphabetic string by reversing the character shift.\"\"\"\n        return \"\".join(\n            chr(((ord(ch) - ord(\"a\") - self._shift) % 26) + ord(\"a\"))\n            for ch in text\n        )\n\n```python\n# filename: src/shift_cipher/repositories/file_repository.py\nimport os\nimport tempfile\nfrom ..exceptions import FileRepositoryError\n\n\nclass FileRepository:\n    \"\"\"Handles reading from and writing to plain text files with specified encoding.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, encoding: str = \"utf-8\"):\n        self.encoding = encoding\n\n    def read(self, path: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Reads the content of a file and returns it as a string.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            with open(path, \"r\", encoding=self.encoding) as f:\n                return f.read()\n        except OSError as e:\n            raise FileRepositoryError(f\"Error reading file '{path}': {e}\")\n        except UnicodeDecodeError as e:\n            raise FileRepositoryError(f\"Encoding error reading file '{path}': {e}\")\n\n    def write(self, path: str, contents: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Writes content to a file using an atomic write pattern.\"\"\"\n        dirpath = os.path.dirname(path) or \".\"\n        try:\n            # Ensure the directory exists\n            os.makedirs(dirpath, exist_ok=True)\n            # Use tempfile.mkstemp for atomic writes\n            fd, tmp_path = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=dirpath)\n            with os.fdopen(fd, \"w\", encoding=self.encoding) as fh:\n                fh.write(contents)\n            os.replace(tmp_path, path) # Atomically replace the target file\n        except OSError as e:\n            # Attempt to clean up temp file if os.replace fails\n            if os.path.exists(tmp_path):\n                os.remove(tmp_path)\n            raise FileRepositoryError(f\"Error writing to file '{path}': {e}\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            if os.path.exists(tmp_path):\n                os.remove(tmp_path)\n            raise FileRepositoryError(f\"An unexpected error occurred while writing to '{path}': {e}\")\n\n```python\n# filename: src/shift_cipher/services/cipher_service.py\nfrom ..models import CipherRequest, CipherResult\nfrom ..services.encoder import EncoderService\nfrom ..services.decoder import DecoderService\nfrom ..repositories.file_repository import FileRepository\nfrom ..utils.validation import validate_lowercase_alpha, sanitize_input\nfrom ..exceptions import ValidationError\n\n\nclass CipherService:\n    \"\"\"Orchestrates validation, encoding/decoding operations, and optional persistence.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, encoder: EncoderService, decoder: DecoderService, repo: FileRepository):\n        self._encoder = encoder\n        self._decoder = decoder\n        self._repo = repo\n\n    def encode(self, req: CipherRequest) -> CipherResult:\n        \"\"\"Validates input, encodes text, and optionally persists the result.\"\"\"\n        sanitized_input = sanitize_input(req.input_text)\n        if not validate_lowercase_alpha(sanitized_input):\n            raise ValidationError(\"Input must be a non-empty string containing only lowercase alphabetic characters (a-z).\")\n\n        encoded_text = self._encoder.encode(sanitized_input)\n\n        if req.output_path:\n            self._repo.write(req.output_path, encoded_text)\n\n        return CipherResult(result_text=encoded_text, input_length=len(sanitized_input), mode=req.mode)\n\n    def decode(self, req: CipherRequest) -> CipherResult:\n        \"\"\"Validates input, decodes text, and optionally persists the result.\"\"\"\n        sanitized_input = sanitize_input(req.input_text)\n        if not validate_lowercase_alpha(sanitized_input):\n            raise ValidationError(\"Input must be a non-empty string containing only lowercase alphabetic characters (a-z).\")\n\n        decoded_text = self._decoder.decode(sanitized_input)\n\n        if req.output_path:\n            self._repo.write(req.output_path, decoded_text)\n\n        return CipherResult(result_text=decoded_text, input_length=len(sanitized_input), mode=req.mode)\n\n```python\n# filename: src/shift_cipher/controllers/cli_controller.py\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Sequence, Optional\nfrom ..services.cipher_service import CipherService\nfrom ..models import CipherRequest\nfrom ..exceptions import ShiftCipherError, ValidationError, FileRepositoryError\nfrom ..config import Config\n\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Parses command-line arguments and maps them to CipherService operations.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, cipher_service: CipherService):\n        self._cipher_service = cipher_service\n        self._config = Config() # Use default config for CLI messages etc.\n\n    def _parse_args(self, argv: Optional[Sequence[str]]) -> argparse.Namespace:\n        \"\"\"Parses CLI arguments using argparse.\"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            prog=self._config.cli_name,\n            description=\"Encode or decode lowercase alphabetic strings using a Caesar-style shift cipher.\"\n        )\n\n        subparsers = parser.add_subparsers(\n            dest=\"mode\",\n            required=True,\n            help=\"Operation mode (encode or decode)\"\n        )\n\n        # Common arguments for encode/decode\n        common_parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(add_help=False)\n        input_group = common_parser.add_mutually_exclusive_group(required=True)\n        input_group.add_argument(\n            \"-t\", \"--text\",\n            type=str,\n            help=\"Direct input string (lowercase a-z only)\"\n        )\n        input_group.add_argument(\n            \"-f\", \"--file\",\n            type=str,\n            help=\"Path to an input file (UTF-8, lowercase a-z only)\"\n        )\n        common_parser.add_argument(\n            \"-o\", \"--output\",\n            type=str,\n            help=\"Path to an output file (UTF-8); if not provided, output to stdout\"\n        )\n\n        # Encode sub-command\n        encode_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\n            \"encode\",\n            parents=[common_parser],\n            help=\"Encode input text by shifting characters forward by 5 positions.\"\n        )\n        encode_parser.set_defaults(mode=\"encode\")\n\n        # Decode sub-command\n        decode_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\n            \"decode\",\n            parents=[common_parser],\n            help=\"Decode input text by shifting characters backward by 5 positions.\"\n        )\n        decode_parser.set_defaults(mode=\"decode\")\n\n        return parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n    def run(self, argv: Optional[Sequence[str]]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Executes the CLI logic based on parsed arguments.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            args = self._parse_args(argv)\n            input_text = \"\"\n\n            if args.text:\n                input_text = args.text\n            elif args.file:\n                input_text = self._cipher_service._repo.read(args.file) # Access repo via service\n\n            request = CipherRequest(\n                input_text=input_text,\n                mode=args.mode,\n                output_path=args.output\n            )\n\n            if args.mode == \"encode\":\n                result = self._cipher_service.encode(request)\n            else: # args.mode == \"decode\"\n                result = self._cipher_service.decode(request)\n\n            if not args.output:\n                print(result.result_text)\n            return 0 # Success exit code\n\n        except ValidationError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: {e.message}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2 # Validation error exit code\n        except FileRepositoryError as e:\n            print(f\"File Error: {e.message}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 3 # File I/O error exit code\n        except ShiftCipherError as e:\n            print(f\"Application Error: {e.message}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1 # Generic application error\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1 # Catch-all for unexpected errors\n\n```python\n# filename: src/shift_cipher/app.py\nfrom typing import Optional, Sequence\nfrom .config import Config\nfrom .services.encoder import EncoderService\nfrom .services.decoder import DecoderService\nfrom .repositories.file_repository import FileRepository\nfrom .services.cipher_service import CipherService\nfrom .controllers.cli_controller import CLIController\n\n\ndef main(argv: Optional[Sequence[str]] = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Main entry point for the Shift Cipher application.\"\"\"\n    config = Config()\n    file_repository = FileRepository(encoding=config.default_encoding)\n    encoder_service = EncoderService(shift=config.max_shift)\n    decoder_service = DecoderService(shift=config.max_shift)\n    cipher_service = CipherService(\n        encoder=encoder_service,\n        decoder=decoder_service,\n        repo=file_repository\n    )\n    cli_controller = CLIController(cipher_service=cipher_service)\n    return cli_controller.run(argv)\n\n```"}
